  <abstract format="text/plain" language="en" script="Latn">Recommendation ITU-T X.1101 defines the network and service models used for multicast communication. It addresses potential security threats and the required countermeasures. Potential threats are defined from the general, mobility-oriented and multicast specific perspectives, and multicast-specific threats are analysed in particular detail. As such, the security requirements, framework and functions are defined and explained as the main focus of the Recommendation.</abstract>
